A lambda expression is a short way to represent an anonymous function (method without name).

It is mainly used to implement functional interfaces.

Introduced in Java 8.

🔹 Functional Interface

An interface that contains only ONE abstract method.

Example
interface Demo {
    void show();
}

✔ Can have multiple default & static methods
✔ Must have only one abstract method

🔹 Basic Syntax
(parameters) -> { body }
Examples
() -> System.out.println("Hello");
(a, b) -> a + b;
(int a) -> { return a * a; }

